Title: Tremont Temple
Order: 2
Production Code: 1x02

INT. TREMONT TEMPLE - NIGHT

AMB: a packed concert hall settling into its seats

[[Reuel Briggs]] and [[Aubrey Livingston]] take their seats in the first balcony. Reuel is distracted, uneasy, still carrying the afternoon's vision with him.

CHARLIE VANCE
(leaning over, grinning)
The soprano soloist is meant to be something, gentlemen. Heard her in New York.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
That explains your presence here, Vance. What's her name?

CHARLIE VANCE
Dianthe Lusk.

MUSIC: IN - an organ prelude, fading to silence

The singers file onto the platform. The opening hymn ends to thunderous applause, and then a soloist steps forward alone into the light.

MUSIC: a single soprano voice, rising

DIANTHE LUSK
(singing)
Go down, Moses, way down in Egypt's land — tell ol' Pharaoh, let my people go.

Reuel goes rigid. The hall, the crowd, all of it falls away for him.

REUEL BRIGGS
(under his breath)
It can't be.

Onstage, [[Dianthe Lusk]] finishes to a hushed, overwhelmed silence, then thunderous applause. As the lights catch her face fully for the first time, Reuel stares — this is the face from the storm.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
By Jove. Briggs — Briggs, are you well?

Reuel doesn't answer. He can't look away.

MUSIC: OUT
